Notes: WORKING COPY revised 20 October 2026, 2:26 AM ET, by George's standing orders in docs/STANDING-ORDERS-2026-10-20.md. Clean original script/dacaveman-skit.md is not edited. The PDF is stale; do not use it. George cut "Watch me!" and Tom's transformation. Dan rips his own shirt and is the only one shirtless. The salon TV plays the Scene 2 Caveman News broadcast when they walk in. One voice per person.

===

DACAVEMAN

> FADE IN:

EXT. MOUNTAIN - TREEHOUSE - DAY

A house is built into a tree on the side of a mountain. Tall windows open onto the living room. Vaulted ceilings. Chandeliers. Clean wooden floors. Luxurious couches. A large flat-screen television is mounted on the wall.

DAN DACAVEMAN hangs off the side of the house. He is five foot five, strong and chiseled, with a superior muscular build, bright eyes in deep sockets, a nice face, thick eyebrows, a beard and goatee, and sharp teeth. His legs and thighs are heavily muscled. A cloth covers his waist, his buttocks, and his genitals. His fingernails and toenails are super long, razor sharp, thick, and ancient.

A rope dangles beside him. It looks as if the rope is holding him. It is not. His toenails are embedded in the tree. He is putting the finishing touches on the house.

TOM DACAVEMAN, the other caveman, stands below and stares up at his father.

TOM
Come on pop. At least hook the rope to your carabiner, for the allusion of safety.

DAN
You being serious right now?


> DISSOLVE TO:

INT. DAN'S HOUSE - LIVING ROOM - DAY

Dan sits in his chair, in pajamas, listening to the news. Past his right shoulder: a large fireplace, an old medieval crock pot, and a pig on a rotisserie.

NEWS ANNOUNCER (ON TV)
This just in, the illegal Alien Ban has been lifted. All aliens in the U.S. and across the globe are considered legal. You are all free to--

He pauses.

NEWS ANNOUNCER (ON TV)
be you!

MONTAGE - ON THE TELEVISION

El Salvadorian immigrants dance.

Jamaican immigrants dance.

Chinese, Ukrainian, and Russian immigrants dance across the world.

END MONTAGE


> CUT TO:

INT. TOM'S PLACE - DAY

Tom sits watching the same broadcast. He blinks. The look on his face is surprise. He calls his father.

INTERCUT -- PHONE CONVERSATION

TOM
(into phone)
Happy born day pops. What you up to?

DAN
(into phone)
You know me son, sittin around relaxing.

TOM
(into phone)
Let's go out to eat. Got a birthday surprise for you.

DAN
(into phone)
You know I hate going out in public.

TOM
(into phone)
Get dressed. I'm on my way.


> CUT TO:

EXT. DAN'S HOUSE - DAY

Tom arrives and honks the horn.

Dan comes out dressed for the winter. Heavy coat, hat, boots, gloves, and scarf. His hair is growing out of his hat. His beard is long. He hops in the car. They drive off.


> CUT TO:

INT. CAR - DAY

TOM
We ain't been out.

DAN
You know I hate going out in public.

TOM
Pop, I wouldn't ask you to go out if it wasn't ok.

Dan looks serious.

DAN
So, you mean, it passed?

TOM
Everyone's excited!

DAN
They have every reason to be.

TOM
To celebrate, how bout a mani-pedi?

DAN
Always wondered about those. What do they do?

TOM
Well, two good looking women work on your feet and hands at the same time while massaging your calf muscles.

DAN
Sounds good. I'm overdue to be pampered. Then, can we eat?

TOM
Just sit back and enjoy the show.


> CUT TO:

EXT. NAIL SALON - DAY

They arrive at the shop.


> CUT TO:

INT. NAIL SALON - CONTINUOUS

A wide picture window. In front of it, leather chairs raised on a step. Each chair has a spa for the feet, with water running. The same kind of chairs sit on the lower level.

A display holds nail tips in various colors.

The television on the wall is already playing the Caveman News broadcast from Scene 2. The same announcer is on camera. The bug reads CAVEMAN NEWS. The story is the ban being lifted. The lower third is readable. It is playing, not a still. It stays on, low under the room, the whole time they are inside.

Dan and Tom walk in with that broadcast behind them. They check in at the front desk. The ancient, long, sharp claws on their hands and feet are covered. Two people stand behind them, dressed in shorts and T-shirts.

The SHOP WORKER behind the counter is a woman in a blue nurse outfit. Her hair is short, dark, and medium-long.

SHOP WORKER
Hello. Can I get the name for the appointment?

TOM
Tom, and Dan DaCaveman.

SHOP WORKER
Have a seat right here.

She directs them to the raised chairs at the picture window. They sit. Dan takes off the hat, scarf, gloves, and coat. He still has a shirt on. Tom never takes his flannel shirt off.

People outside begin to gather at the window, looking into the Spa. The Caveman News broadcast is still playing.

DAN
Wow, son! I feel good.

TOM
Told you. This one of the best feelings in the world. To have women rub and pamper you.

Tom looks at his dad.

TOM
Be comfortable. We don't have to hide anymore. It's the law.

DAN
Everything?

TOM
Everything, Pop.

Tom does not strip. He does not transform.

Dan rips his own shirt off in one move. His chest, shoulders, and arms are bare. A cloth covers only his waist down to his upper thighs. He is fully shirtless. Tom's flannel stays on.

People let out a gasp.

People outside run to the windows in a panic. Surprise is on their faces.

INSERT - DAN'S HANDS AND FEET

His fingernails are as long as his fingers. His toenails are prehistorically thick, in the running water.

BACK TO SCENE

DAN
Ah, it's good to finally give my feet some air!

People outside the store take videos and pictures of Tom and Dan.

Tom, still in his flannel, looks at his father in amazement. He is still looking.

DAN
What's wrong son?

TOM
You could've left some clothing on.

Two guests get up and run out.

DAN
My fir got me covered.

He pats his chest hair. He is still the only one without a shirt.

The person next to them throws up a little in their mouth.

EMPLOYEE ONE and EMPLOYEE TWO come out to work on the two of them. They notice people getting up and abruptly leaving. They stop in front of Tom and Dan.

EMPLOYEE ONE
How are you guys doing ohh my God!

Employee One jumps back.

Employee Two has a look of fear and confusion.

EMPLOYEE TWO
What the hell am I looking at?

Employee One panics and walks in a circle.

EMPLOYEE ONE
We gotta close the shop! We gotta close the shop!

The OWNER runs out in haste and almost falls.

OWNER
Are you freakin kidding me! The ban hasn't even been lifted for twenty-fours yet. I thought you guys only come out at night!

DAN
I know that song! The freaks come out at night! Nope, me and my son here for the free mani-pedi, it's my birthday.

The owner looks at them in disgust. He takes deep gulps.

OWNER
That's nasty.

He pulls out a bullhorn and yells toward the back of the shop.

OWNER
Get me a chisel, a sander and a hazmat bucket. Better make it two hazmat buckets, a few face shields and some thick rubber gloves!

EMPLOYEE ONE
Naw man! One of y'all gonna have to pay!

OWNER
You can't say that!

EMPLOYEE ONE
What you mean? We can close the shop for the week on this ticket alone!

Employee One and Employee Two work on Tom and Dan's nails. They are uncomfortable. Dan is still shirtless. Tom is still in his flannel. The owner checks in another woman.

She sees the two cavemen. She takes a deep breath. She transforms into herself, a CAVEWOMAN. Sackcloth covers her chest, and covers her from the waist to the middle of her thighs. The nails on her hands and feet are the same as Tom's and Dan's. She stays fully covered.

CAVEWOMAN
It's my birthday!

> FADE OUT.
